"""Simon Pearson, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 6, epilogue 1907).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/simon/ and cov/simon/m/): character page "Simon Pearson"
(Background, Events of Red Dead Redemption 2, Mission Appearances, Quotes, Trivia, Gallery captions); FR page
"Simon Pearson" (fr.txt); transcripts "Outlaws from the West/dialogues", "The Aftermath of Genesis/dialogues", "Old
Friends/dialogues", "Eastward Bound/dialogues", "Who is Not Without Sin/dialogues", "Blessed are the
Peacemakers/dialogues", "The Battle of Shady Belle" (.dlg); mission pages "Further Questions of Female Suffrage" (no
transcript on the wiki, checked Oct 2026), "Blessed are the Peacemakers" (story: Pearson helps carry Arthur), "The
Battle of Shady Belle", "Horsemen, Apocalypses" (burial of Kieran), "Fleeting Joy", "That's Murfree Country", "Money
Lending and Other Sins VI & VII" (trivia: Strauss thrown out at night), "My Last Boy" (trivia: no longer at camp),
"Our Best Selves" (Dutch's announcement), "Banking, The Old American Art" (trivia: not at the heist), "Ending
Credits", "American Venom/dialogues" (credits list); companion activity page "Hunting (Simon Pearson)"; wiki pages
"Camp Events" (Shady Belle mood, Beaver Hollow: no Pearson event listed), "Rhodes General Store" (A.J. Banks in
1899, Pearson by 1907), "Ethel Pearson" (unseen, heard upstairs; told too much while drunk; second wife). Real
world: Wikipedia "List of Red Dead Redemption 2 characters" (m/wp_list.txt), which summarizes the official guide
(Price 2018, p. 376) for his family and his arrival out west.
Cross-checked against the fact-checked parts arthur_A, dutch_A, hosea_A, charles_A/B, susan_A/B, sadie_A/B, bill_A,
karen_A, uncle_A, kieran_A, abigail_A: Dutch hands the Colter and Shady Belle camps to Pearson and Susan; Pearson
throws Arthur the can of salted offal; Hosea calls the parley a trap; Dutch answers "It's a bit late for apologies"
(paraphrased here, quoted in part C); Arthur and John clear Shady Belle of Lemoyne Raiders; Milton's three days are
conditional on Dutch giving himself up (Pearson's presence at that scene is not documented, so he is not placed
there); Charles, Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran (mission page version); Susan shoots Molly at the end of chapter 5
and has Bill and Pearson burn the body; Dutch announces at the start of "Our Best Selves" that Uncle, Pearson and
Mary-Beth have run off and calls them cowards (departure not shown); Karen is also gone after "My Last Boy".

Ownership: personality, the official descriptions (Rockstar, September 6, 2018; official guide wording), names
(Mr. Pearson, "fat man", the mail alias Tacitus Kilgore), appearance (tattoo, outfits, 1907 look), skills and the
crafting upgrades, and camp scenes (Sean and the accordion songs, Uncle and the sea stories, Susan and the self-pity
scene, Bill's punch, Micah's money, Hosea and Tahiti, Abigail on the dock, Mary-Beth asking about Kieran, the drunk
song in the rain, Sadie's cleaver row beyond the mission itself, Strauss and the Shady Belle complaints) go to part
B; this part refers to them in one clause at most. Part A OWNS the backstory he tells (whalers, Navy, the fifty days
at sea, the loan sharks), the missions, the 1907 store and the facts about Ethel. Lines quoted in part C are
paraphrased here without quotation marks (the food count, the fifty days, the rum, the "cornered tiger" report,
"What about me?", the apology, "Somebody had a good time", the 1907 line on the Grays and the Braithwaites).

Excluded: the character page's claim that Pearson, Mary-Beth and Uncle tell Tilly they are leaving to save
themselves (no mission page or transcript shows the departure: Dutch's announcement only); "leave together"
(unsupported); the FR wiki's "sans prévenir personne" (unsourced); the "plague" ship (the transcript only gives
fifty days stranded; the camp scene speaks of hunger and disease, used with that wording); "Dutch, Arthur and Hosea
are all very skeptical" (only Hosea's "It's a trap" and Dutch's doubts are in the transcript); "Arthur and Pearson
skin two deer" (the transcript shows Arthur skinning one at Pearson's request); "outside the stables" (the transcript
places the talk in the shed where Pearson cooks); "It can also be assumed that he lives in Scarlett Meadows"
(assumption); the year "prior to 1897" for the loan sharks (no source given on the page; kept vague); Bessie's
absence from the gang photograph and the dating of the photo (speculation on another page); Pearson's role during
the Shady Belle attack and in "A Strange Kindness", "Visiting Hours" and "My Last Boy" (listed by the wiki but not
described on any page: listed in part C only); the claim that he "kept" the photograph since 1899 (only its presence
in 1907 is shown).
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date of birth for Simon Pearson. He served briefly in the United States Navy: Rockstar's 2018 description speaks of a short stint in the navy, and an official guide of a short stint at sea (both texts, with his family of whalers, are quoted under Personality). In his stories in camp and on the crayfish trip with [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]], he names Java and Bali among the places he saw; the Red Dead Wiki adds Sumatra. He tells Arthur that his ship was once stranded at sea for fifty days.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent aucune date de naissance pour Simon Pearson. Il a brièvement servi dans la marine des États-Unis : le texte publié par Rockstar en 2018 parle d'un passage éclair dans la marine, un guide officiel d'un court séjour en mer (ces deux textes, qui évoquent aussi sa famille de baleiniers, sont cités dans la partie Personnalité). Dans ses récits au camp et pendant la sortie aux écrevisses avec [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]], il cite Java et Bali parmi les endroits qu'il a vus ; le Red Dead Wiki y ajoute Sumatra. Il raconte à Arthur que son navire est un jour resté bloqué en mer pendant cinquante jours.")},
    {"p": two("The official guide says he later got into serious trouble out west with men who were extorting money from him. The Red Dead Wiki identifies them as loan sharks and says [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] and his gang got him out of their hands. He then became the gang's cook and butcher.",
              "Le guide officiel indique qu'il s'est ensuite attiré, dans l'Ouest, de graves ennuis avec des hommes qui lui extorquaient de l'argent. Le Red Dead Wiki y voit des usuriers et précise que [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] et sa bande l'ont tiré de leurs griffes. Il devient alors le cuisinier et le boucher de la bande.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("After the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater, the gang flees north into the mountains and takes shelter in Colter, an abandoned mining town, during a snowstorm. In \"Outlaws from the West\", when Davey Callander's body is carried into the cabin, Susan hands out the first jobs and tells Pearson to see what food is left. Dutch then addresses the group and asks Pearson and Miss Grimshaw to turn the place into a camp, since they may be there for a few days.",
              "Après l'échec du braquage du ferry à Blackwater, la bande fuit vers le nord, dans les montagnes, et se réfugie à Colter, une ville minière abandonnée, en pleine tempête de neige. Dans \"Outlaws from the West\", quand le corps de Davey Callander est porté dans la cabane, Susan distribue les premières tâches et charge Pearson de faire l'inventaire de la nourriture. Dutch prend ensuite la parole et demande à Pearson et à Miss Grimshaw de transformer l'endroit en camp, car ils risquent d'y rester quelques jours.")},
    {"p": two("In \"The Aftermath of Genesis\", Pearson tells Arthur, in the shed where he cooks, that a few cans and a rabbit are all he has to feed ten or twelve people. He starts a story about the Navy, which Arthur tries to cut short. He explains that he could not get supplies in before the flight from Blackwater, and that he sent [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] and [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] hunting but they found nothing. Arthur replies that the gang will survive, and if need be will eat the cook, the fattest of them. [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]], who has come in, ends the argument and takes Arthur hunting despite his burnt hand. Before they leave, Pearson throws Arthur a can of assorted salted offal for the road.",
              "Dans \"The Aftermath of Genesis\", Pearson explique à Arthur, dans la remise où il cuisine, qu'il n'a que quelques conserves et un lapin pour nourrir dix ou douze personnes. Il entame une histoire de marine qu'Arthur tente d'écourter. Il précise qu'il n'a pas pu faire de provisions avant la fuite de Blackwater, et qu'il a bien envoyé [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] et [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]] chasser, mais qu'ils n'ont rien trouvé. Arthur répond que la bande survivra et qu'au besoin, on mangera le cuisinier, le plus gras de tous. [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]], entré entre-temps, coupe court à la discussion et emmène Arthur chasser malgré sa main brûlée. Avant leur départ, Pearson lance à Arthur une boîte d'abats salés assortis pour la route.")},
    {"p": two("On the way out, Charles says Pearson does not know what he is talking about and that there is game in the hills. The two men kill two deer. On the way back, Arthur points out to Charles that the cook has been drinking since the flight from Blackwater and left without any food. At the kitchen they find [[uncle|Uncle]] drinking with Pearson, and Arthur sends him away. Pearson shares his Navy rum with Arthur and Charles, then asks Arthur to help with the skinning. Arthur skins one of the deer. Pearson asks him to bring him anything else he catches, and Arthur asks him in return to make a good stew.",
              "À l'aller, Charles affirme que Pearson ne sait pas de quoi il parle et qu'il y a du gibier dans les collines. Les deux hommes abattent deux cerfs. Au retour, Arthur fait remarquer à Charles que le cuisinier boit depuis la fuite de Blackwater et qu'il est parti sans rien à manger. À la cuisine, ils trouvent [[uncle|Uncle]] en train de boire avec Pearson, et Arthur le congédie. Pearson partage son rhum de la marine avec Arthur et Charles, puis demande à Arthur de l'aider à dépecer. Arthur dépèce l'un des cerfs. Pearson lui demande de lui rapporter tout ce qu'il chassera, et Arthur lui demande en retour de préparer un bon ragoût.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Old Friends\", Dutch leads Arthur and several other men to raid the O'Driscoll hideout at Ewing Basin. Before leaving, he asks Pearson, [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] and Charles to look after Colter, since there are O'Driscolls about. In \"Eastward Bound\", when the snow thaws, Pearson loads supplies onto the wagons while [[abigail-marston|Abigail]] and Charles help the injured [[john-marston|John Marston]] into one of them. He rides in the lead wagon with Dutch on the way down to Horseshoe Overlook, near Valentine. Once the new camp is set up, Dutch tells everyone to get to work, and Pearson speaks up from the crowd: the gang needs real food, and someone has to bring it in every day.",
              "Dans \"Old Friends\", Dutch emmène Arthur et plusieurs autres hommes attaquer la planque des O'Driscoll à Ewing Basin. Avant de partir, il demande à Pearson, à [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] et à Charles de surveiller Colter, car des O'Driscoll rôdent dans le secteur. Dans \"Eastward Bound\", au dégel, Pearson charge les provisions dans les chariots pendant qu'[[abigail-marston|Abigail]] et Charles installent [[john-marston|John Marston]], blessé, dans l'un d'eux. Il voyage dans le chariot de tête avec Dutch jusqu'à Horseshoe Overlook, près de Valentine. Une fois le nouveau camp monté, Dutch ordonne à tous de se mettre au travail, et Pearson prend la parole depuis le groupe : la bande a besoin de vraie nourriture, et quelqu'un doit en rapporter chaque jour.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("At Horseshoe Overlook, Pearson works from his chuck wagon (see Skills). In \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur carries a drunk [[orville-swanson|Reverend Swanson]] back into camp, and Pearson is one of the gang members who comment as they pass, with a remark about someone having had a good time. At the end of the chapter, after a shootout in Valentine, Dutch decides to move on, and in \"A Strange Kindness\" Arthur comes back to find the camp being packed up. The gang settles at Clemens Point, on Flat Iron Lake in Lemoyne, near Rhodes.",
              "À Horseshoe Overlook, Pearson travaille depuis son chariot-cuisine (voir Compétences). Dans \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur ramène au camp le [[orville-swanson|révérend Swanson]], ivre, et Pearson fait partie de ceux qui lâchent un commentaire à leur passage, en notant que quelqu'un s'est bien amusé. À la fin du chapitre, après une fusillade à Valentine, Dutch décide de partir, et dans \"A Strange Kindness\", Arthur rentre au camp alors que tout le monde plie bagage. La bande s'installe à Clemens Point, au bord du lac Flat Iron, en Lemoyne, près de Rhodes.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("At Clemens Point, [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] has been helping Pearson in the kitchen. In \"Further Questions of Female Suffrage\", Arthur comes across the two of them in a heated argument: Sadie refuses to spend her days cooking and reminds Pearson that she and her husband shared the work on their ranch. Arthur offers to take her into Rhodes to buy supplies for the kitchen. Before they leave, Pearson gives Arthur a letter to post, addressed to his aunt Cathy, in which he describes his adventures and his success in life. On the way, Sadie opens the letter and reads it aloud in an imitation of him. Back at camp, Arthur and Sadie help Pearson unload the wagon.",
              "À Clemens Point, [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] aide Pearson en cuisine. Dans \"Further Questions of Female Suffrage\", Arthur tombe sur eux en pleine dispute : Sadie refuse de passer ses journées aux fourneaux et rappelle à Pearson qu'elle et son mari se partageaient le travail du ranch. Arthur propose de l'emmener à Rhodes acheter des provisions pour la cuisine. Avant leur départ, Pearson lui confie une lettre à poster, adressée à sa tante Cathy, où il raconte ses aventures et sa réussite. En chemin, Sadie ouvre la lettre et la lit à voix haute en l'imitant. De retour au camp, Arthur et Sadie aident Pearson à décharger le chariot.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] calls Pearson over and, when Dutch joins them, pushes him to explain himself. Pearson says that he met a couple of O'Driscolls on the road into town, that a fight nearly broke out, and that they ended up suggesting a parley between Dutch and [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]] to end the feud. Dutch asks whether they have lost their minds, and Hosea calls it a trap. Micah insists it is worth the risk, and Dutch agrees to go with him, with Arthur covering them with a rifle. Pearson asks whether he can come too, and Dutch turns him down.",
              "Dans \"Blessed are the Peacemakers\", [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] appelle Pearson et, quand Dutch les rejoint, le pousse à s'expliquer. Pearson raconte qu'il a croisé deux O'Driscoll sur la route de la ville, que la situation a failli dégénérer et qu'ils ont fini par proposer des pourparlers entre Dutch et [[colm-odriscoll|Colm O'Driscoll]] pour mettre fin à la querelle. Dutch leur demande s'ils ont perdu la tête, et Hosea parle d'un piège. Micah insiste : le risque vaut d'être pris. Dutch accepte d'y aller avec lui, Arthur les couvrant au fusil. Pearson demande s'il peut venir, et Dutch refuse.")},
    {"p": two("The parley is a trap: the O'Driscolls capture Arthur, who escapes and rides back to Clemens Point badly hurt. When he collapses in camp and tells Dutch it was a set-up, Pearson apologizes to him, and Dutch replies that it is too late for apologies. Pearson then helps carry Arthur to his tent. After \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\" and the visit of the Pinkerton agents [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] and [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]], the gang leaves for Shady Belle, an abandoned plantation house in the bayou near Saint Denis. In \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", Arthur and John clear the house of the Lemoyne Raiders who occupy it. When the caravan arrives, Dutch asks Miss Grimshaw and Mr. Pearson to work their magic on the new camp.",
              "Les pourparlers sont un piège : les O'Driscoll capturent Arthur, qui s'échappe et revient à Clemens Point grièvement blessé. Quand il s'effondre au camp en disant à Dutch que c'était un coup monté, Pearson lui présente ses excuses, et Dutch répond qu'il est un peu tard pour ça. Pearson aide ensuite à porter Arthur jusqu'à sa tente. Après \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\" et la visite des agents de la Pinkerton [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] et [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]], la bande part pour Shady Belle, une demeure de plantation abandonnée dans le bayou, près de Saint-Denis. Dans \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", Arthur et John chassent de la maison les Lemoyne Raiders qui l'occupent. À l'arrivée du convoi, Dutch demande à Miss Grimshaw et à M. Pearson d'opérer leur magie sur le nouveau camp.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("Pearson dislikes the swamp, and at Shady Belle he complains about it to several gang members (see Relationships). After \"Angelo Bronte, A Man of Honor\", he invites Arthur on a companion activity the Red Dead Wiki calls \"Hunting\". The two men row from Shady Belle into the swamp to the east and search the water for crayfish. Pearson then spots alligators near their nests and draws them away while Arthur gathers their eggs.",
              "Pearson n'aime pas le marais, et à Shady Belle il s'en plaint à plusieurs membres de la bande (voir Relations). Après \"Angelo Bronte, A Man of Honor\", il propose à Arthur une activité de compagnon que le Red Dead Wiki intitule \"Hunting\". Les deux hommes partent en barque de Shady Belle vers le marais situé à l'est et fouillent l'eau à la recherche d'écrevisses. Pearson repère ensuite des alligators près de leurs nids et les attire ailleurs pendant qu'Arthur ramasse leurs œufs.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", the O'Driscolls send [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]]'s mutilated body into the camp on a horse and attack Shady Belle. Once they are driven off, Dutch has Charles, Reverend Swanson and Pearson bury Kieran, while Arthur and John clear away the bodies of the attackers. Pearson takes no part in the bank robbery in Saint Denis that ends the chapter: the mission page lists him among the gang members who do not appear in it.",
              "Dans \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", les O'Driscoll renvoient au camp, sur un cheval, le corps mutilé de [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]], puis attaquent Shady Belle. Une fois les assaillants repoussés, Dutch charge Charles, le révérend Swanson et Pearson d'enterrer Kieran, pendant qu'Arthur et John évacuent les cadavres des assaillants. Pearson ne participe pas au braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis qui clôt le chapitre : la page de la mission le range parmi les membres de la bande qui n'y apparaissent pas.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("While Dutch, Arthur and the survivors of the robbery are stranded on Guarma, the rest of the gang moves to Lakay, a group of shacks in the bayou. According to the Red Dead Wiki's character page, he and Abigail are the ones who greet Arthur at Lakay in \"Fleeting Joy\". Milton's Pinkertons attack Lakay soon after, and the gang moves again, to Beaver Hollow, a cave in Roanoke Ridge.",
              "Pendant que Dutch, Arthur et les rescapés du braquage sont bloqués à Guarma, le reste de la bande s'installe à Lakay, un ensemble de cabanes dans le bayou. D'après la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, c'est avec Abigail qu'il accueille Arthur à Lakay, dans \"Fleeting Joy\". Les Pinkerton de Milton attaquent Lakay peu après, et la bande déménage de nouveau, à Beaver Hollow, une grotte de Roanoke Ridge.")},
    {"p": two("In \"That's Murfree Country\", the scene that closes the chapter, Uncle brings a drunk [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] into the new camp. She claims to have informed the Pinkertons about the Saint Denis robbery, and Susan kills her with a shotgun. Susan then tells Bill and Pearson to burn the body.",
              "Dans \"That's Murfree Country\", la scène qui clôt le chapitre, Uncle ramène au nouveau camp une [[molly-oshea|Molly O'Shea]] ivre. Elle prétend avoir renseigné la Pinkerton sur le braquage de Saint-Denis, et Susan l'abat d'un coup de fusil. Susan ordonne ensuite à Bill et à Pearson de brûler le corps.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("According to the page of \"Money Lending and Other Sins VI & VII\", if Arthur throws [[leopold-strauss|Leopold Strauss]] out of Beaver Hollow at night, Pearson and Susan, who sleep next to him, wake up frightened and move out of the way when Arthur pushes Strauss toward their beds, where Strauss packs his bag. Pearson is among those who later ask Arthur about Strauss's disappearance. According to the Red Dead Wiki's character page, he drinks more and more in this chapter and sees no way out for the gang.",
              "D'après la page de \"Money Lending and Other Sins VI & VII\", si Arthur chasse [[leopold-strauss|Leopold Strauss]] de Beaver Hollow en pleine nuit, Pearson et Susan, qui dorment à côté de lui, se réveillent effrayés et s'écartent quand Arthur pousse Strauss vers leurs lits, où celui-ci fait son sac. Pearson fait partie de ceux qui interrogent ensuite Arthur sur la disparition de Strauss. D'après la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, il boit de plus en plus dans ce chapitre et ne voit plus d'issue pour la bande.")},
    {"p": two("After \"My Last Boy\", Pearson is no longer at the camp, nor are Uncle, [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] and [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]]. The game does not show them leaving. At the start of \"Our Best Selves\", Dutch tells Arthur that Uncle, Pearson and Mary-Beth have run off and calls them cowards; Arthur answers that they do not want to die.",
              "Après \"My Last Boy\", Pearson ne se trouve plus au camp, pas plus qu'Uncle, [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] et [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]]. Le jeu ne montre pas leur départ. Au début de \"Our Best Selves\", Dutch annonce à Arthur qu'Uncle, Pearson et Mary-Beth ont pris la fuite et les traite de lâches ; Arthur répond qu'ils ne veulent pas mourir.")},

    # ================================================================ Epilogue 1907
    {"h3": two("Epilogue (1907)", "Épilogue (1907)"), "year": "1907"},
    {"h4": two("Epilogue: Rhodes", "Épilogue : Rhodes"), "chapter": "E2"},
    {"p": two("By 1907 Pearson owns the general store in Rhodes, in Scarlett Meadows, which A.J. Banks ran in 1899. He is now married to Ethel (see Relationships). A photograph of the Van der Linde gang posing on a stagecoach hangs on the wall near his counter.",
              "En 1907, Pearson est propriétaire du magasin général de Rhodes, dans les Scarlett Meadows, que tenait A.J. Banks en 1899. Il est désormais marié à Ethel (voir Relations). Une photographie de la bande Van der Linde, posant sur une diligence, est accrochée au mur près de son comptoir.")},
    {"p": two("[[john-marston|John Marston]], who now lives with his family on a ranch at Beecher's Hope, can visit the store several times; the Red Dead Wiki counts four conversations. Pearson is glad to see him, and each congratulates the other on his new life: John on the shop, Pearson on the ranch. John tells him that he still sees Uncle, [[charles-smith|Charles]] and [[sadie-adler|Sadie]]. Pearson admits that he once told Ethel too much about the gang while drunk. He also mentions the Grays and the Braithwaites, the two feuding families the gang dealt with in 1899 (see Quotes).",
              "[[john-marston|John Marston]], qui vit désormais avec sa famille dans un ranch à Beecher's Hope, peut passer au magasin à plusieurs reprises ; le Red Dead Wiki recense quatre conversations. Pearson est heureux de le revoir, et chacun félicite l'autre pour sa nouvelle vie : John pour la boutique, Pearson pour le ranch. John lui apprend qu'il voit toujours Uncle, [[charles-smith|Charles]] et [[sadie-adler|Sadie]]. Pearson avoue avoir un jour trop parlé de la bande à Ethel, après avoir bu. Il évoque aussi les Gray et les Braithwaite, les deux familles rivales auxquelles la bande a eu affaire en 1899 (voir Citations).")},
    {"p": two("The end credits of the game, which follow \"American Venom\", include a scene in the store. Pearson finishes serving a customer, who leaves. He walks back to his register, takes a breath and looks at the photograph of the gang on the wall with a slight smile.",
              "Le générique de fin du jeu, qui suit \"American Venom\", comprend une scène dans le magasin. Pearson termine de servir un client, qui s'en va. Il retourne à sa caisse, prend une inspiration et regarde, avec un léger sourire, la photographie de la bande accrochée au mur.")},
]
